This is a right-facing overhead pass to a teammate off-screen on image-right. The basketball is separately rendered by the game. Both hands remain empty; never draw a ball, sphere, orb, seams, court, hoop, rim, floor, ground shadow, background, glow, border, grid, text, teammate or opponent. Every exterior and gutter pixel must be true alpha-zero transparency, with no checkerboard, matte, speckles or color haze.

Six sequential distinct full-body poses:
0 composed ready stance, elbows relaxed and empty hands at chest level;
1 gathers the invisible ball and lifts both hands above his forehead, eyes tracking image-right;
2 extends both empty hands overhead, weight shifting into a measured step;
3 RELEASE at simulation tick5: both arms extend high and toward image-right, wrists open after the overhead lob leaves his hands, keeping his face and long hair unobscured;
4 overhead follow-through with fingers extended and lead foot planted;
5 recovers to an upright composed stance as both arms lower naturally, hands empty.

Leo remains right-facing. Keep every pose anatomically plausible, complete and consistent in face, long wavy hair, mustache, pale skin, black/crimson kit and shoes. Return only the transparent sprite sheet.
